userStories.description:
**Goal** — Add and export the pure, one-level alias reference helper without wiring any callers yet.

**Motivation** — Custom tiers cannot carry this: a tier entry cannot reference another name, tiers are per agent with default-agent fallback, and turning a pin into a tier changes escalation behaviour (#2977).

**Approach** — A reference is `@<name>` or `@<name>[<effort>]`, matched against the whole string: `<name>` is one or more characters that are not whitespace, `[` or `]`, and the optional suffix is exactly one trailing `[<effort>]` with a non-empty effort that holds no whitespace or brackets. Any other string that starts with `@` (`@sol[high`, `@sol[]`, `@sol[a][b]`, `@sol[high]x`, `@ sol`) is a malformed reference. Before lookup the pass treats a missing or non-object `agent.modelAliases` as `{}` and a non-string alias value as an invalid alias, so a malformed map produces `MODEL_ALIAS_INVALID`, never a crash. Expansion looks `<name>` up in the alias map with an own-property check. A reference without a suffix yields the alias value unchanged. A reference with a suffix yields the alias value's base id (`parseModelSpec(value).model`) followed by `[<effort>]`, replacing any suffix the value carried, the same rule `withEffort` applies to tier selectors (`src/config/schema-types.ts`).

The pass reads the alias map from `raw.agent.modelAliases` (absent: `{}`), matching each reference against the keys as trimmed, the same way `ModelAliasesSchema` trims them. The helper owns this matching rule so direct CLI callers get the same result. `ModelAliasesSchema` (`src/config/schemas-model-alias.ts`): `z.record(z.string().trim().min(1), ModelAliasTargetSchema)`; a value is `provider/model[effort]` (`MODEL_ALIAS_TARGET`) or `acp:<agent>[/<model>][effort]` (`ACP_ALIAS_TARGET`). Referenced values must be literal provider/model ids in this feature's config/override positions, not acp: targets, aliases, bare ids, tiers or lists.

All expansion errors are `NaxError` with code `MODEL_ALIAS_INVALID` and context `{ stage: "config", path, alias }`. Error text is `<path>: <message>`. Required messages: `unknown model alias "name"`; `model alias "name" must be a literal model id, not another alias`; `model alias "name" is an acp: target, usable only from agent files`; `model alias "name" is not a provider/model id`; `empty model alias reference` for `@` or `@[high]`; `malformed model alias reference "<ref>"` for malformed nonempty references. Use the shared parseModelSpec API for suffix replacement; the map's target shape is not broadened.

**Scope** — In: create src/config/model-alias-expand.ts and its helper unit tests; export MODEL_ALIAS_PREFIX and expandModelAliasRef from src/config/index.ts. Out: US-002's recursive config walker and aggregation, US-003's load/schema wiring, US-004's CLI consumers, and US-005's guide. Alias chaining and agent-file @ syntax are not introduced.

**Interface** —
```typescript
export const MODEL_ALIAS_PREFIX = "@";

/** One `@name[effort]` reference -> the literal id it stands for. Throws MODEL_ALIAS_INVALID. */
export function expandModelAliasRef(
  ref: string,
  aliases: Readonly<Record<string, string>>,
  path: string, // config path or "--model", named in the error
): string;
```
